# 3.2.scenario.disentangle.correlation.anecdotes.stone

## .what

weight each scenario against the case's exposures from the **anecdote corpus** — forward and
backtrack correlations over the itemized owner-reports. biased and high-recall; kept apart from the
formal base rate on purpose.

## .inputs

- `2.2.scenario.enumeration.from.literature.yield.md` — the social corpus gathered in phase 2
- `2.3.scenario.enumeration.blend.yield.md` — the lineup

## .do

- itemize the corpus into one tagged row per case (exposure(s), effect, outcome)
- compute **forward**: P(effect | exposure alone) over the corpus
- compute **backtrack**: P(exposure | effect) over the corpus
- treat every forward number as an **upper bound**, not a rate (selection/problem-skew)
- flag co-occurrence confounds (mixed exposures) — do not attribute a mixed case to one exposure

## .emit

into `3.2.scenario.disentangle.correlation.anecdotes.yield.md` — forward + backtrack per scenario,
each flagged upper-bound.

## .done when

each scenario carries a forward + backtrack anecdote signal, all upper-bound-flagged, confounds noted.
